Hi everyone,

I'm keen to release an update of the RSQLServer <https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer> package to CRAN in the next few weeks (v0.2). You can read the NEWS <https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/blob/master/NEWS.md> for what has changed. But the key features are:

1. An implementation of a SQL backend for dplyr compatibility.
2. A much better (and backward incompatible) change to the dbConnect interface
3. Azure-hosted SQL Servers are now supported.
3. A working example is now provided in the README <https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/blob/master/README.md>.

For those of you who use this package, could I ask you to install and test this (both the DBI methods and the dplyr support)? Please report any bugs or unexpected behaviour on Github <https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/issues>.

I am looking to build out a test framework by v0.3.

Thanks!

